<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gustav Adolph, Duke of Mecklenburg-Güstrow</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1633–1695</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gustav Adolph was the last Duke of Mecklenburg-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gustrow">Güstrow</a>, reigning from 1636 under a regency and in person from 1654 until his death in 1695. A Lutheran ruler, he rebuilt a land devastated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War. He died without surviving sons, and the dispute over his inheritance was settled by the Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamburg">Hamburg</a> in 1701, which created Mecklenburg-Schwerin and Mecklenburg-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strelitz">Strelitz</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gustav-adolph-duke-of-mecklenburg-gustrow.jpg" alt="Gustav Adolph, Duke of Mecklenburg-Güstrow" width="320" height="395" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unidentified painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gustav_Adolf_von_Mecklenburg-G%C3%BCstrow.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
